  page1: [
    "The NeanderBros belong to the land of Az’Kalon, and they have a distant memory of their lesser god as the “Ancient One.” Their empire expanded beyond the continent and encompassed nearby islands. These islands were colonies that maintained trade with the mainland, but they could also support themselves for long periods of time if necessary. The NeanderBros, at the zenith of their imperial might, had long since left behind magic in favor of technology, but, in ways which they could not entirely perceive, magic was an important element of their technology.",
    "The fall of the empire was caused by civil war. In the pursuit of their technology, the NeanderBros took two different directions: creation and destruction. Those on the side of creation developed their technology based on the magic of Az’Kalon and the Ancient One, though they were unaware of these magical and supernatural aspects; they only knew they were in harmony with what",
  ],
  page2: [
    "encouraged the life of organisms and the well-being of the land. The other faction–those on the side of destruction–developed technology that exploited life and the land. Mastery over death became their obsession. They believed this mastery could only be achieved by destroying the limitations of life, so they sought to use death as the tool for their transcendence.",
    "The results of the civil war were the split of the NeanderBros on the continent into the Shamans and the Zombies, and the NeanderBros on the colonies stayed away when they heard of the civil war. They had cultures of their own, were mostly self-sufficient, and did not want to risk their lives. The colonies now ignored the continent because they didn’t want to inadvertently recreate the supremacy it once exercised over them. Only one colony tried to re-establish contact after centuries of silence",
    "Being from the most remote colony, they were the descendants of the bravest of the NeanderBros who set out to expand the empire so long ago, hoping to escape the rigid society of the homeland for better opportunities abroad. Now, the sons of the rejected were coming back to reclaim their fatherland and make it anew. They wanted to forge a second empire, greater than the last. One that wouldn’t be bound by the dead traditions and cold austerity of the fallen one. They would incorporate the colonies on the basis of fairness and equality and usher in a true golden age for the NeanderBros.",
    "However, events did not transpire as intended. This far-flung colony of NeanderBros reached their ancestral fatherland, but the land they re-discovered ",
  ],
  page3: [
    "NeanderBros do have females–NeanderGals. In their ancient history, they were the ones most attuned to magic, so, naturally, this evolved into the NeanderGals being the ones who developed and innovated technology. This resulted in the NeanderGals being the heart of NeanderBro society. Due to the intensity of such labor, the males oversaw and ran most of their civilization’s functions, and it was left to them to develop techniques to best exploit the technology given them by their wives.",
    "Technology evolved from magic because the NeanderBros wanted greater",
  ],
  page5: [
    `capable of being domesticated, and still others made for good hunting.  The land had an abundance of crystals that came to be used as a kind of currency between the four tribes which developed from the returning colonists.
    As the Outcast NeanderBros spread, some chose to remain where they first landed, in the verdant southern region with its teeming wetlands and azure coasts (the PaleoBros). Others elected to settle the flinty mountains and caverns of the central portion of Az’Kalon (the RockBros). A third group preferred the forests in the far west with all of`,
    `their towering trees, stirred by the invigorating breath of the strong western wind (the BirdBros). Lastly, there was a group which decided to make its dominion the placid lakes and calming rivers of the north (the MerBros).`,
    `Unbeknownst to the Outcast NeanderBros, the very land of Az’kalon is suffused with the magic of the Ancient One, hence why each group was adapted to its region. The power of the land molded the NeanderBros to itself. Only the northeast was unsettled, for the NeanderBros learned quickly to leave it be. Multiple parties from the four tribes tried to explore that region and none returned, but creatures from that region soon began to appear throughout the land, attacking and killing in the lands of the four tribes of the NeanderBros.`,
  ],
  page11: [
    "An accidental discovery made by two members of the PaleoBro people would alter the destiny of all Az’Kalon. Zindar and Tibaran earned fame in their tribe by discovering a piece of the portal-device. They were trying to determine the nature of the beasts invading from the north and were tracking a pack of smaller ones and found them digging in an area on the outskirts of their territory. They remained hidden and watched until a faint purple light began to emanate from the ground. The beasts went wild and removed a golden object that was the source of the light. It seemed to have a brief effect on the weather itself.",
    "The noon sun dimmed, and the wind changed direction; unfortunately for the brothers-in-arms, their scent was carried to the beasts, and a brutal fight ensued. They killed many of the beasts and stole their coveted golden fragment, but, no matter how far they traveled away from the dig-site, they were continually pursued. It didn’t take much to deduce that these beasts somehow could sense the object, so Zindar and Tibaran made it back to their village, and the women, who are magic-users and scientists, placed the object in a sealed container and submerged it in the bottom of a lagoon as a temporary solution until a plan could be devised.",
    "They theorized the light was calling out to the beasts and that they could diminish its power by covering it with layers of darkness, but this would not keep the creatures away forever. The Elder PaleoGals were gathered and the fragment was brought to them. They studied it for twenty-four hours without rest, and the PaleoBros were standing watch in case any beasts appeared. The fragment was ordered to be contained and sunk to the bottom of the lagoon again by the Elder PaleoGals.",
    "Their judgment was that the fragment could not be destroyed by anything they",
  ],
